  "chapter": {
    "number": 88,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(89) A Psalm of instruction for Aetham the Israelite."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will sing of your mercies, O Lord, for ever: I will declare your truth with my mouth to all generations.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you have said, Mercy shall be built up for ever: your truth shall be established in the heavens.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I made a covenant with my chosen ones, I swore to David my servant.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 163
          },
          {
            "text": "establish your seed for ever, and build up your throne to all generations. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The heavens shall declare your wonders, O Lord; and your truth in the assembly of the saints.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For who in the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 164
          },
          {
            "text": "heavens shall be compared to the Lord? and who shall be likened to the Lord among the sons of God?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "God is glorified in the council of the saints; great and terrible toward all that are round about him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord God of hosts, who is like to you? you are mighty, O Lord, and your truth is round about you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You rule the power of the sea; and you calm the tumult of its waves.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have brought down the proud as one that is slain; and with the arm of your power you have scattered your enemies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The heavens are your, and the earth is your: you have founded the world, and the fullness of it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have created the north and the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 165
          },
          {
            "text": "west: Thabor and Hermon shall rejoice in your name.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Your is the mighty arm: let your hand be strengthened, let your right hand be exalted.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Justice and judgment are the establishment of your throne: mercy and truth shall go before your face.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed is the people that knows the joyful sound: they shall walk, O Lord, in the light of your countenance.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And in your name shall they rejoice all the day: and in your righteousness shall they be exalted.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you are the boast of their strength; and in your good pleasure shall our horn be exalted,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "for our help is of the Lord; and of the Holy One of Israel, our king.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Then you spoke in vision to your children, and said, I have laid help on a mighty one; I have exalted one chosen out of my people.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have found David my servant; I have anointed him by my holy",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 166
          },
          {
            "text": "mercy.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For my hand shall support him; and my arm shall strengthen him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The enemy shall have no advantage against him; and the son of transgression shall not hurt him again.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And I will hew down his foes before him, and put to flight those that hate him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But my truth and my mercy shall be with him; and in my name shall his horn be exalted.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 25,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And I will set his hand in the sea, and his right hand in the rivers.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 26,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He shall call upon me, saying, You are my Father, my God, and the helper of my salvation.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 27,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And I will make him my firstborn, higher than the kings of the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 28,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will keep my mercy for him for ever, and my covenant shall be firm with him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 29,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And I will establish his seed for ever and ever, and his throne as the days of heaven.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 30,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If his children should forsake my law, and walk not in my judgments;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 31,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "if they should profane my ordinances, and not keep my commandments;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 32,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will visit their transgressions with a rod, and their sins with scourges.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 33,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But my mercy I will not utterly remove from him, nor wrong my truth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 34,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Neither will I by any means profane my covenant; and I will not make void the things that proceed out of my lips.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 35,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Once have I sworn by my holiness, that I will not lie to David.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 36,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "His seed shall endure for ever, and his throne as the sun before me;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 37,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and as the moon that is established for ever, and as the faithful witness in heaven. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 38,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But you have cast off and set at nothing, you have rejected your anointed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 39,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have overthrown the covenant of your servant; you have profaned his sanctuary, casting it to the ground.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 40,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have broken down all his hedges; you have made his strong holds a terror.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 41,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "All that go by the way have spoiled him: he is become a reproach to his neighbors.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 42,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have exalted the right hand of his enemies; you have made all his enemies to rejoice.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 43,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have turned back the help of his sword, and have not helped him in the battle.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 44,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have deprived him of",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 167
          },
          {
            "text": "glory: you have broken down his throne to the ground.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 45,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have shortened the days of his",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 168
          },
          {
            "text": "throne: you have poured shame upon him. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 46,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "How long, O Lord, will you turn away, for ever? shall your anger flame out as fire?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 47,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Remember what my being is: for have you created all the sons of men in vain?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 48,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What man is there who shall live, and not see death? shall any one deliver his soul from the hand of Hades? Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 49,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Where are your ancient mercies, O Lord, which you swore to David in your truth?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 50,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Remember, O Lord, the reproach of your servants, which I have borne in my bosom, even the reproach of many nations;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 51,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "wherewith your enemies have reviled, O Lord: wherewith they have reviled the recompense of your anointed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 52,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed be the Lord for ever. So be it, so be it.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
